      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "You are a coding assistant helping a student complete a JavaScript filter function for a movie app.\n\nThe student is learning how filters work by using `.map()`, an `if` statement, and `.push()`.\n\nThe app uses:\n\n- `movies`\n- `displayMovies`\n- `renderMovies()`\n- `filterActionMovies()`\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Reset `displayMovies` to an empty array\n- Use `.map()` to go through each movie in `movies`\n- Use an `if` statement to check whether `movie.genre === \"Action\"`\n- Use `.push()` to add matching movies to `displayMovies`\n- Call `renderMovies()` at the end\n- Use `filterActionMovies` as the event handler for the **Action** button\n- Use the existing button id: `filterActionBtn`\n\nExample of correct structure:\n\n```js\nconst filterActionMovies = () => {\n  displayMovies = [];\n\n  movies.map((movie) => {\n    if (movie.genre === \"Action\") {\n      displayMovies.push(movie);\n    }\n  });\n\n  renderMovies();\n};\n\ndocument.getElementById(\"filterActionBtn\").addEventListener(\"click\", filterActionMovies);"
      }
    },
    "project_template_level_name": "ai-generated-design-lesson8-level2_template_2026",
    "long_instructions": "## **Complete the Action Filter**\r\n\r\nWhen the user clicks **Action**, only movies with the genre **Action** should appear.\r\n\r\n#### **Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Use AI to help you complete the `filterActionMovies` function.\r\n\r\n2. In the function, use `.map()` to go through each movie in `movies`.\r\n\r\n3. Inside the `.map()`, use an `if` statement to check whether the movie’s genre is `\"Action\"`.\r\n\r\n4. If the movie’s genre is `\"Action\"`, use `.push()` to add that movie to `displayMovies`.\r\n\r\n5. Call `renderMovies()` as the last line of the `filterActionMovies` function.\r\n\r\n6. Use your function as the event handler for the **Action** button.\r\n",
